            <ArticleTitle>Isolated torsion of the fallopian tube as differential diagnosis to acute abdominal pain in a thirteen year old girl.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>229-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Authors illustrate a case of torsion of the Fallopian tube in a young girl not yet sexually active. Even though this pathology is very rare in childhood and early puberty, torsion of the fallopian tube should be considered as a possible differential diagnosis in intermittent abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
